        "y0": 0.7890142517814727,
        "x1": 0.9006067226890756,
        "y1": 0.8323883610451306
      },
      "text": "as the diﬀerential map on ﬁnite levels OLTsm → ΩLT1,sm, and deﬁne d|π−1OFℓ to be the zero map. By Theorem 0.3.1, for any U ∈ BLT such that zd = 0 on U, we may write any section s ∈ OLT(U) of the form for some suﬃciently large n:",
